exp_24: wire the repaired rank-1 driver and make the ladder survive a slow instrument B

Three fixes found by inspecting the two tools the parent pushed, before spending
hours of GPU time on them:

- build_crosscheck filtered instrument B's popcorn files on a `benchmark`
  filename prefix, but run_rank1_bench3.sh names its files after its pass label
  (warm/test/bench), not after the eval.py mode. Every rank-1 number would have
  been silently dropped. It now skips only test-mode files, which carry no timing
  blocks, and flags rank-1's JIT-warming pass as throwaway so it cannot become
  the headline.
- The rank-1 cross-check arm now calls the repaired tools/run_rank1_bench3.sh,
  which performs all three passes itself in the mandatory warm -> test -> bench
  order. Its four repairs are verified mechanically before use and disclosed in
  result.md 8.8 with the behaviour-preserving argument: they change only how the
  arm is launched, never what it computes.
- Aggregation now runs twice, once the moment instrument A finishes and again
  after B, so a long or dead instrument B cannot take a completed six-shape
  ladder down with it at the --expect-b assertion.

The run is detached behind tools/gpu_lease.sh with an exit trap, since the queue
wait alone can exceed an hour and the ladder several more.
